**`repository.py`:**
- Import: `from shared.audit import AuditLog` and `from modules.auth.models import User`
- `async def get_audit_entries(db, skip, limit, filters: dict | None) -> tuple[list, int]`
  - Query `AuditLog` LEFT JOIN `User` on `AuditLog.changed_by == User.id`
  - Select: all AuditLog columns + `User.full_name` as `user_name`
  - Apply filters: `entity_type`, `entity_id`, `action`, `changed_by`, `date_from` (timestamp >=), `date_to` (timestamp <=)
  - Order by `AuditLog.timestamp` DESC
  - Return (list of results, total count)
- `async def get_entity_audit(db, entity_type, entity_id, skip, limit) -> tuple[list, int]`
- `async def get_user_audit(db, user_id, skip, limit) -> tuple[list, int]`
- `async def get_audit_stats(db) -> dict`
  - Count by action (GROUP BY action)
  - Count by entity_type (GROUP BY entity_type)
  - Top 5 most active users (GROUP BY changed_by, ORDER BY count DESC, JOIN users for name)

**`service.py`:**
- Wraps repository calls
- `generate_description(action, entity_type, old_values, new_values) -> str`
  - CREATE: "Created {entity_type}" + name/serial if in new_values
  - UPDATE: "Updated {entity_type}" + list of changed field names
  - DELETE: "Deleted {entity_type}" + name/serial if in old_values
  - STATUS_CHANGE: "Changed {entity_type} status from X to Y"
  - RESOLVE: "Resolved {entity_type} error"
  - Default: "{action} on {entity_type}"
- Applies description to each entry before returning

